ICML 2026 Paper (typage/icml) - license

This template contains files from two sources.

  main.tex, refs.bib, manifest.json, typage.json, LICENSE
      Written by 7D24H. CC0-1.0: dedicated to the public domain; papers
      written from this template need no attribution.
      https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

  icml2026.sty, icml2026.bst, fancyhdr.sty, algorithm.sty, algorithmic.sty
      The official ICML 2026 style kit, published by the International
      Conference on Machine Learning for authors preparing submissions, in
      https://media.icml.cc/Conferences/ICML2026/Styles/icml2026.zip
      icml2026.sty carries no license statement (rights remain with ICML).
      icml2026.bst (Hal Daume III, generated with makebst by Patrick W Daly)
      and fancyhdr.sty are under the LaTeX Project Public License, as stated
      in their headers. algorithm.sty and algorithmic.sty (Peter Williams,
      1994; algorithmic modified by Alex Smola, 2000) carry a copyright notice
      and no license statement. All five files are redistributed unmodified,
      as ICML publishes them, so that the template compiles offline.

The packages the sample loads (natbib, hyperref, ...) come from the
built-in Tectonic bundle under their own licenses. Check
https://icml.cc for the rules that apply to your submission.
